t.textos.atrahasis.pasajes.2.texto:
When the fourth year came, their cities were in distress,
their broad […] became narrow (?);
the people wandered dejected through the streets.
When the fifth year came, the daughter awaited the mother's coming in;
the mother does not open the door to her daughter;
the daughter watches the scales of the mother,
the mother watches the scales of the daughter.
When the sixth year came, they prepared the [daughter] for a meal,
they prepared the child for food (?); full was […].
One house devoured another;
like (?) […] their faces were veiled;
the people lived with bated breath.
[…]
Above, Adad diminished his rain,
below it was held back [so that the flood did not rise from the springs].
The field diminished its yield;
the womb of Nisaba changed: at night the fields were white;
the broad plain brought forth salt;
the plant did not sprout, the lambs did not grow fat.
Calamity was laid upon mankind;
the womb was closed, no child came forth.
